{
 "game": "rbr",
 "title": "Richard Burns Rally (RallySimFans) car names, engines and gearing",
 "keys": "name is the RSFCarID as a string: the car key is rbr/<RSFCarID>, the one Oversteer makes from the install's Cars/Cars.ini [Car05] (rbr_install.car_in_slot). screen_name is RSF's name of the car. `names` lists every car RSF's car list (rsfdata/cache/cars.json) has, with the facts cars_data.json holds (path, year, drivetrain, gear count); `cars` only those whose NGP physics have been on the install.",
 "notes": "Derived numbers only, read from RSF's physics files of the cars on marth's install, 2026-10-26; built by research/rbr/car_table.py. torque_curve: [rpm, Nm], the engine's full-load torque: the normalised curve (Tq_NN_NGP, 0..1) times the peak torque RSF lists for the car (cars_data.json), cut at the limiter; the curve peaks at the listed rpm. limiter_rpm: ControlUnit RPMLimit (the rpm the Fiesta was seen to reach is 0.5 % above it). gear_sets: one per distinct default setup (gravel, tarmac, snow; the surfaces that share one are joined in its id), gravel the default; gears are the setup's GearId entries 2.. (GearId0 is reverse, 1 neutral) as GearList Gear / Pinion teeth. final_drive: the setup's DropGearId entry, whose pair is stored the other way (Pinion / Gear: 35 / 8 = 4.375 on the Fiesta); a set whose drop gear differs carries the quotient in `primary`, so the overall ratio is gear x primary x final_drive. transfer_ratio: the FinalDriveId entry (Gear / Pinion, 62 / 63 on the Fiesta): NOT in the overall ratio, the Fiesta's and i20's captures fit without it to 0.3 %. The player's own setup may change the drop gear (DropGearOptions): the overall ratio then differs, the steps between gears (the best upshift) do not. gearbox_efficiency: 1 - DriveTrainLoss_NGP / 100. tyre_radius_m: EffWheelRadius (one value for every surface). auto_upshift_rpm: ControlUnit GearNUpshift for 1st.. (the AI's automatic gearbox). mass_kg: 1 / InverseMass. A slot folder of rsfdata/Physics counts only where a file named after the RSF car marks it; the others hold stock Richard Burns Rally cars and are not shipped. Verified on the Fiesta WRC 2019 against marth's captures of 2026-10-26 (docs/richard-burns-rally.md).",
